Every morning, Oliver would rise before the sun, his footsteps echoing through the quiet halls of the hospice. He was meticulous in his work, ensuring that each patient's room was spotless, their belongings arranged with care, and their emotional needs attended to. His gentle touch and soothing voice were like a balm to the weary souls who resided within the hospice's walls.

Oliver had a unique ability to read between the lines, sensing when a patient needed a simple touch, a listening ear, or a shared laugh. He would often spend hours sitting by their bedside, sharing stories of his own past, or simply holding their hand, offering a silent presence that spoke volumes.

